{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-121086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=-2xy.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y>0$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-121086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-2x$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n \nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/fa7402608c175237bfed11ddf032d867a0685e2ad5cf31f848809f796b705780.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>0$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-121086" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3164315862af2309076c3a4ae2bfe33535f58892d2cc5690b2d16bb48f54b74a"} {"question" "q-121086" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-121086" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |"] ["text" "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |"] ["text" "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |"] ["text" "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |"] ["text" "| $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-121086" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y)=-3xy.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\ge 0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-3x$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/3cfdf7d548c430f225a78fa6c4d915d69207f0a1c090d13cdd530c90865731ef.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3164315862af2309076c3a4ae2bfe33535f58892d2cc5690b2d16bb48f54b74a"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/058a4ec5eba7a1ada3fc5b89ada73819672a19f88fbf4450d1b2c04a4b0db498.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/29cf79e3f216a3b33656473fd98bd04252e2abd6304fdd575ee56cd33e1f4c3d.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9ca3a2fd93541dd1865f95beb53cddeb3ff1e7759e1534ae547c4b943931d24e.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/ba965b75553f65311903910e182eac9c7b49e4acdf28f79db8712a113051c464.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/e4fb6cb6b35a80a392e6f5091fddb7c136996927ea1810f0dd1db5d0e263996c.png"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-121252" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9ca3a2fd93541dd1865f95beb53cddeb3ff1e7759e1534ae547c4b943931d24e.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-149610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y)=-{x}^{2}y.$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\ge 0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-149610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/c35c98904d2a0d0d6d49c582cd9f9dba9d96e91ae0da5deb2d329f38f77532e3.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/9340582eaad37c4ce1e0c8cbcdce48faec1e36c3c05adbedd61aa2de7168fd2f.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-{x}^{2}$ | $y$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n\n  \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/assets/17dd9e10234b6a69123241a882e267d95d505d1944d7c31ef563f9ac06b990af.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14038247/state.json" "file_sha256" "29deb74e43ae81462e9d65d83baf4a89c30e89fc7b92ab71d079f62a98dda607"} {"question" "q-149610" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :ques